1
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,980
Somehow it'll work out.

2
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,960
Look, even Akaneru is burning up.

5
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:18,280
Somehow, eventually, it'll work out.

6
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,520
You understand, right? Got it, got it.

7
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:27,420
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:43,400
I'll teach you ninja techniques.

9
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:59,040
This show's been really popular lately,
hasn't it?

10
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:02,900
What they're doing is just like ninja training,
you know.

11
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:06,860
If you get it right, you win

12
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:14,780
What's wrong, senpai? Hearing about a real ninja,
I was almost reminded of someone. The method...

13
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:25,480
If it's a ninja you want, I'm right here! A dog
talking... You understand human language, hohoho.

14
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:27,280
It's me, it's me!

15
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,520
Even if you say "me"...

16
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:31,000
It's the old man from Volvo!

17
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:35,620
That's right,
Volvo-san's grandfather was a real ninja.

18
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:37,840
So he's using ninjutsu.

19
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:41,680
Excuse me. This is the ninja art of summoning,
the kuchiyose no jutsu!

20
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:45,360
He's hiding somewhere and talking.
Where is he?

21
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:47,360
What?

22
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:25,820
Didn't he? Tokyo's more profitable, so... Does
Mr. Big Volvo know that it's easy to understand?

23
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:32,140
That's because he got lost on his way to that guy's house.
I followed the map exactly, I did.

24
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:40,160
Which map? Mine, or the welcome-year one?

25
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:40,600
Me

26
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,840
That's the Volvo's room over there.

27
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:55,340
He should be home today,
since he just got off his night shift.

28
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,060
Let's try contacting him.

29
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:59,240
No, there's no need for that.

30
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,400
But...

31
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:03,400
Going into the Volvo's house without permission is dangerous,
you know.

32
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:06,500
The other day,
they tried to break into the Volvo's room.

33
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:08,260
That gang of burglars did.

34
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:25,540
They fell into the trap the Volvos
set and were caught all at once.

35
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:29,300
I see right through his character.

36
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,460
So striking first is the sure way to win.

37
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:33,880
First, smoke bombs.

38
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,060
He's in a total panic, isn't he?

39
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:41,740
Quick, with this!

40
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:48,560
Isn't that going too far?

41
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,320
That much is fine.

42
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:03,780
Insolent little thing!

43
00:05:03,780 --> 00:05:07,180
This is my ninjutsu technique!

44
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:13,540
Yay! No matter what, that's going too far!

45
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:22,960
Mr. Volvo! It's the old man!
The old man from Kyushu!

46
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,903
Oh no! That Volvo guy

47
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:31,400
has completely switched into battle mode!

48
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:33,500
Can't we stop him somehow?

49
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:36,000
There's no choice, I'll handle this myself!

50
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:42,900
Hey, what on earth did you do?

51
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:47,120
Yeah. It's the Ninja Nude
Playing Card Technique.

52
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:49,400
How is that ninjutsu at all?

53
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:53,540
What? You're opening
a ninja school in Tokyo?

54
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:57,140
Yeah. I was thinking of borrowing your room.

55
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:01,220
What a mess this is.
Clean up once in a while.

56
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:03,420
Grandpa,
you're the one who made this mess just now.

57
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:07,280
But running a ninja school in
this room just isn't possible.

58
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:12,400
Fine, I'll just buy land
myself and build a classroom.

59
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,200
You should have done that from the start.

60
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:16,320
What's the budget?

61
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,520
Don't fall over in shock.

62
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:21,840
It's three million!

63
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,460
Too shocked to even speak?

64
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:29,800
Nakagawa, show him the reality.

65
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:33,020
Even if land prices have dropped,

66
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:35,380
W-what?!

67
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:42,140
I never imagined land prices were that high.

68
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:45,000
Grandpa, don't lose heart.

69
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,600
What are you doing all of a sudden?

70
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:52,260
A ninja must never let his guard down,
not even for a moment.

71
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:52,820
Yes.

72
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:58,040
But land prices are that high?

73
00:06:58,860 --> 00:06:59,380
I'm defeated.

74
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:03,060
Look, I'm down in the dumps like this.

75
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:06,220
Couldn't you at least
try to console me a little?

76
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:08,560
That's because you went and threw something.

77
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:11,780
I'll look for a classroom space on my end.

78
00:07:11,780 --> 00:07:12,900
Really?

79
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:15,060
It might have to be a rental, though.

80
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:18,520
Thank heavens, thank heavens.

81
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:20,140
Good for you, Gramps.

82
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:23,240
Nice dodge.

83
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,240
Well done!

84
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:26,320
That look just now was serious.

85
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:32,540
Here.

86
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:36,020
We bought a cheap derelict building
that was about to be torn down.

87
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,600
It's perfect for classes, isn't it.

88
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:39,780
Wait!

89
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:40,320
What?

90
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:45,920
So there really was a trap.

91
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,720
What a dangerous old geezer.

92
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:50,920
Gramps, I brought Reiko and the others.

93
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:51,540
What?

94
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:01,680
You came!

95
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:04,760
Congratulations on the
opening of the school.

96
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:06,420
Thank you, thank you.

97
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:09,380
You've got the vitality of a cockroach.

98
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:13,080
Don't say that.

99
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,980
Let me show you around the school.

100
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:20,860
This is the ninja museum.

101
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:22,660
This is just a gift shop!

102
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:25,840
It's the same as the house
in Kyushu I visited before.

103
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,780
They even sell books.

104
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:29,260
It's exactly the same, isn't it?

105
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:32,680
This time, sell the new shuriken too.

106
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,740
What's new about this?

107
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:36,920
It's just a regular shuriken!

108
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:39,780
It's coated with luminous paint,

109
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:41,940
so you can tell at night that it's glowing.

110
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:43,500
It's like a flare.

111
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:47,120
Even in night battles,
there's no risk of friendly fire.

112
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:49,200
It'd look like an enemy, too, you know.

113
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,900
This one's the latest ninja model,
after all.

114
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:54,420
First, it quickly changes
into a kitchen knife.

115
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:56,240
It can even sharpen pencils.

116
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:58,240
It also has a bottle opener.

117
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,140
And a can opener.

118
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:01,260
Gesoline.

119
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:03,460
Put the two sheets
together and it's scissors.

120
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:05,360
And a compass.

121
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:06,280
How about that?

122
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,020
Tie-in, right?

123
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:09,220
The 10-in-1 Knife is still better.

124
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,440
Sorry.

125
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,760
My hand just slipped.

126
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:13,640
You did that on purpose.

127
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:17,560
Want some herbal tea?
It's good for your health.

128
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:18,420
Thank you.

129
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:20,180
Wait a second.

130
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:21,460
This pattern.

131
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:22,420
No way.

132
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:25,520
Don't tell me one of the
herbs gives you diarrhea.

133
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:26,680
Sorry.

134
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:27,300
What?

135
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,240
It's training to tell poison apart.

136
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,720
It's like Russian roulette

137
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,880
Well then, I'll just...

138
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:39,640
Wait, wait!

139
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:42,050
I'll choose first.

140
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:45,320
It'd be awful if I got the
one left over at the end.

141
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,080
Alright, this one!

142
00:09:48,980 --> 00:09:50,220
Whoa, it's delicious!

143
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:52,260
Grandpa, that's the one, right?

144
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:52,940
Yeah.

145
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:54,180
Jackpot.

146
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:58,400
What are we going to do? You drank it all!

147
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:02,920
Relax, I've got
diarrhea-stopping herbs ready too.

148
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:07,760
This Gennoshoko decoction
will cure it right up.

149
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:08,900
That'll be 1,500 yen.

150
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:09,900
That's too expensive.

151
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:11,860
Then just enjoy your diarrhea.

152
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:13,480
Fine, fine, I'll buy it.

153
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:18,320
Gramps, isn't this aconite, torikabuto?

154
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:21,440
Sorry, I got careless.

155
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:22,600
That wasn't carelessness.

156
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:26,200
No, maybe it's garlic grass.

157
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:28,820
Actually, I don't really know either.

158
00:10:28,820 --> 00:10:30,860
Don't make me drink an
herb you don't even know!

159
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:32,000
Let's look it up.

160
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:36,600
So it really is poison.

161
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,640
Looking closer, the first one you put in

162
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,660
wasn't a safe herb either.

163
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:44,860
Look it up properly before you add it!

164
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:48,540
I-I'm not thirsty right now, so

165
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:50,640
I'll pass too.

166
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,520
So that means you...

167
00:10:54,180 --> 00:10:56,760
might have been slowly
fed poison all this time!

168
00:10:57,880 --> 00:10:59,740
I don't feel well somehow.

169
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:02,700
I've been fine until now, though!

170
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:04,000
It's fine, it's fine.

171
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:08,260
What, you still have zero students?

172
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:11,440
Even when someone interested
shows up now and then,

173
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:13,760
they apparently quit within an hour.

174
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:14,960
Of course they do.

175
00:11:15,860 --> 00:11:17,440
But that's a bit pitiful, isn't it.

176
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,980
After coming all the way to Tokyo...

177
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:21,920
I'd like to do something for him, somehow.

178
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:28,900
Yes, actually,
I don't have a single student yet.

179
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:32,900
Please, be my first student.

180
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,200
Why me?

181
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:38,860
Without students, it's not a school.
Please, please, please!

182
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:41,320
Stop it, don't get your face so close!

183
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:44,780
Just do it, Ryo-chan. The old man's pitiful.

184
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:47,100
I'll make the tuition free.

185
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:48,920
Even if you say that...

186
00:11:50,340 --> 00:11:53,880
I'll give you ten percent of the tuition
from students who enroll in the future.

187
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:59,620
Really? Alright, I understand. I'll enroll.

188
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:03,460
See that?
This is the ninjutsu of forceful persuasion!

189
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:14,080
Two people too, please enroll... No, wait. If we're doing this,
let's have the entire station's staff enroll.

190
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:22,620
You can do that? I see. So you'll have it officially adopted as a martial art,
like kendo or judo.

191
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:26,280
I see, now that you mention it,
that's one way to do it.

192
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:29,920
This could actually turn
out to be quite profitable.

193
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:47,640
Actually, it might be rather interesting
for police officers to learn ninjutsu.

194
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:50,920
Depending on how it's used,
I think it could be useful.

195
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,100
What happened to Ryotsu?

196
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:56,600
Wasn't he supposed to greet
us in front of the school?

197
00:12:57,220 --> 00:12:58,320
That's what was supposed to happen, yes.

198
00:12:59,280 --> 00:12:59,640
What?

199
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:06,540
Where's Ryotsu?

200
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:08,620
I'm right here.

201
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:14,280
This is the Mokuton jutsu!

202
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:16,760
It's useful for tailing
suspects and stakeouts.

203
00:13:17,432 --> 00:13:21,020
I doubt it's actually useful, though.

204
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:23,844
Well, the secret art of
Combat-style ninjutsu,

205
00:13:23,894 --> 00:13:26,960
let me show you thoroughly now.

206
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:27,546
Mm,

207
00:13:27,596 --> 00:13:31,200
By the way, where is this Mr. Kogane-maru?

208
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:36,200
If it were me, it'd be right here.

209
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:37,980
W-where?

210
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:40,280
Where are you looking? Up, up!

211
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:42,060
Up.

212
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:44,418
Ahahaha,

213
00:13:44,468 --> 00:13:48,590
I am the principal of the
Combat-Style Ninja School,

214
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,460
Saigo Kogane-maru!

215
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:52,620
That's dangerous!

216
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:53,990
It's fine,

217
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:56,880
I rode these every day in Kyushu.

218
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:59,260
I'm coming over there now, here goes!

219
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:04,280
Wood Release: Momonga Jutsu

220
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:05,300
Dangerous!

221
00:14:06,020 --> 00:14:07,500
Don't worry.

222
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:17,540
Are you all right? Call an ambulance, quick!

223
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:20,440
No need to worry. It's just a scratch.

224
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:22,540
Then let me get the first-aid kit.

225
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:24,028
I don't need that either.

226
00:14:24,078 --> 00:14:27,520
Ninjas carry their own medicine, you know.

227
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:32,940
Hey, this one says it's
constipation medicine!

228
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:38,900
Then is it this one? Or was it that one?

229
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,280
Maybe this one?

230
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:43,540
You're like a traveling
medicine peddler from Toyama.

231
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:48,940
The medicine just won't come out...
what a hassle.

232
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:52,800
Eat your spinach and
you'll get your energy back.

233
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:58,720
You're just like Popeye, aren't you?

234
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:02,580
Why on earth do you carry medicine around

235
00:15:04,380 --> 00:15:06,000
Well then, this way to the dojo.

236
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:11,680
Now, let me show you a ninja technique.

237
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:13,380
Reiko isn't ready yet!

238
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:15,740
She might be taking her time changing.

239
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:21,120
Damn, just imagining it made my nose bleed.

240
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:26,780
Good, you're done changing, Reiko-san.

241
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:30,980
Gush!

242
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:36,040
Ahhhh! Deco-san, what's with that outfit?

243
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:38,220
Ahhhhh!

244
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:47,960
Disinfecting this spot? It's headless...
where's the mouth supposed to be?

245
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:53,560
A disguise to scout the enemy,
and a way to protect yourself.

246
00:15:55,940 --> 00:15:57,820
And a form that confuses the enemy.

247
00:15:57,820 --> 00:15:59,480
Truly, a kunoichi!

248
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:00,300
I see.

249
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:07,240
It's true, it is an attractive outfit.

250
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:10,760
Some of the female staff might not like it.

251
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:11,700
I see.

252
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:13,520
What a pity.

253
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:14,740
What a pity.

254
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:16,920
No

255
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:27,380
Of all places, the Earth Escape technique.

256
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:33,100
Hide underground and
scout the enemy's movements.

257
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:35,440
It's perfect for infiltration
operations, right?

258
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:38,180
Even if you say underground,

259
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:41,760
there's hardly any ground left in Tokyo.

260
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:49,820
How about the Force Field
and Water Cloud technique?

261
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:52,100
You can cross a river without
getting your clothes wet.

262
00:16:52,540 --> 00:16:54,700
Wouldn't the commote be faster?

263
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:58,080
It looks like it would flip over
if there were even a little wave.

264
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:07,860
If you're going to say that much,

265
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:11,020
I'll show you my special ninjutsu.

266
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:12,980
Are you perhaps going to do that one?

267
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:16,600
Yes, the Ninjutsu Katon technique!

268
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:21,080
It's a technique where I blow fire from
my mouth to make the opponent flinch.

269
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:24,060
It should work on ninjutsu too.

270
00:17:24,060 --> 00:17:27,000
I might expect a little something, but...

271
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:27,900
Here I go,

272
00:17:27,950 --> 00:17:31,040
first I take a special liquid into my mouth.

273
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:34,760
You're like a human pump, aren't you?

274
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:49,540
Not much of a reliable ninja, are you.

275
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:59,920
Let's pretend this
conversation never happened.

276
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:04,620
Ryotsu, you too, stop just playing
around and get serious about your work.

277
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:08,880
Yes, yes, quiet!

278
00:18:10,820 --> 00:18:14,320
What are we supposed to do now?
You ruined a good money-making deal!

279
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:17,660
Even I make mistakes sometimes.

280
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:22,720
But now there's almost no chance
of us being hired by the police.

281
00:18:23,220 --> 00:18:28,060
If only we could actually show how ninjas
are useful for police investigations.

282
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:28,760
Mm.

283
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:33,000
Then why don't we just arrest the
criminals with ninjutsu ourselves?

284
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,440
I see.

285
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:36,020
Good idea.

286
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,900
Shall we get started right away?

287
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:47,860
Are you ready?

288
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:49,500
Anytime.

289
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:50,740
Go!

290
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,940
Nice view up here.

291
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:06,320
Hello?

292
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:07,600
Hey, Kogane-maru-chan.

293
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:10,760
Keep a sharp watch for
anyone suspicious, got it?

294
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:11,940
I know.

295
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:15,080
You should get a little more altitude.

296
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:20,440
Isn't that a bit too high?

297
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,860
There are a lot of tall buildings in Tokyo,
after all.

298
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:24,000
Not nearly enough yet.

299
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:26,160
G-Grandpa...

300
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,520
Hey, do something!

301
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:30,140
Don't worry, I'll do something now.

302
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:33,060
Rinpō, comeback, Maitako-kun!

303
00:19:33,060 --> 00:19:33,480
Da...

304
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,740
Go after him!

305
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:48,020
Where on earth are they
being carried off to?

306
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:53,220
What happened?

307
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:57,820
It's me.

308
00:19:57,820 --> 00:19:59,260
Senior, it's bad!

309
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:03,580
We caught a drug deal in
progress at headquarters, but

310
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:08,820
The gang fled by car! They ran into our building!
Please come back right away!

311
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:11,920
But even if you tell us
to come back right away...

312
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:18,020
Wait! This is the perfect
chance to show off our strength!

313
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:21,240
Nakagawa! What's the suspects' car like?

314
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:23,480
A black sedan! It looks like a foreign car!

315
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:28,640
Ah!

316
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:34,740
That's...!

317
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:37,420
What?

318
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:39,380
They're planning to escape by helicopter!

319
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:41,600
We're catching them no matter what!

320
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:42,880
Volvo!

321
00:20:52,260 --> 00:20:54,040
Damn! Are we not going to make it in time?

322
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:02,660
Go, go!

323
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:05,800
Those octopuses are totally useless,
aren't they?

324
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:11,100
Yes! This is the divine wind!

325
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:14,960
Like hell I'll let them get away!

326
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:15,960
Ugh.

327
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:22,400
Take this!

328
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:28,500
Damn it, Japanese ninjas are no good at all,
it doesn't work!

329
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,440
Aaaaaah!

330
00:21:32,060 --> 00:22:02,040
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooo! No, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

331
00:22:02,060 --> 00:22:22,760
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

332
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:23,180
Congratulations!

333
00:22:25,060 --> 00:22:26,200
You idiot!

334
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:30,211
To bring down a helicopter with shuriken,

335
00:22:30,261 --> 00:22:31,780
ninjutsu is truly terrifying.

336
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:34,180
Hey, hey, what about those jewels?

337
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:36,960
Oh no, could this be a bad feeling?

338
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:45,420
This is my school.

339
00:22:47,620 --> 00:22:49,128
Not this ending again.

340
00:22:49,178 --> 00:22:52,140
And it was such a good
chance to make some money.

341
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:58,520
Doesn't something sound like it's ticking?

342
00:22:59,080 --> 00:23:00,120
Come to think of it,

343
00:23:01,020 --> 00:23:05,820
No! That shock must have
activated the self-destruct switch!

344
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:09,160
Why would you have something
like that installed?!

345
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:10,900
It's standard for ninja.

346
00:23:10,900 --> 00:23:12,540
Disable it right now!

347
00:23:12,980 --> 00:23:15,840
It's too late!
It'll explode in five seconds!

348
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:17,000
Woooaaah!

349
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:35,540
Sure, you did arrest the culprit,
and I'll give you credit for that.

350
00:23:36,100 --> 00:23:40,940
But we've received this many complaints
from the residents around here!

351
00:23:40,940 --> 00:23:42,360
I know, I know.

352
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:45,380
That's why I'm sitting here writing this report,
isn't it?

353
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:49,040
Anyway, where did that grandpa of yours go?

354
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:51,400
He went back to Kyushu a little while ago.

355
00:23:53,760 --> 00:23:55,240
He sure is quick to run away.

356
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:57,780
Wahahahaha!

357
00:23:57,780 --> 00:23:59,040
Ahahahaha!

358
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:01,760
Farewell, I'm off!

359
00:24:14,580 --> 00:24:17,940
Like someone is calling out to me,

360
00:24:18,660 --> 00:24:20,540
an afternoon after the rain.

361
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:27,120
I walked looking back,
led by the hand of the capsule toy machine.

362
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:34,320
That strange feeling I had back then.

363
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:39,540
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

364
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:45,320
I walked only on the black ones.

365
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:53,480
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

366
00:24:54,580 --> 00:25:00,940
Even the politicians with their self-important
faces and the aunties with blue eyeshadow.

367
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:06,520
Try turning that corner over there.

368
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:11,700
You can meet everyone, everyone.

369
00:25:14,140 --> 00:25:16,380
There's a wall over there.

370
00:25:17,520 --> 00:25:19,680
Well, surely there's a wall.

371
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:25,000
Everyone, come to our town!

372
00:25:26,020 --> 00:25:26,460
Thank you.

373
00:25:30,340 --> 00:25:32,160
Wait, you bought a cruiser?

374
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:32,920
I see.

375
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:36,500
I thought I'd make time to connect with nature,
for the kids too.

376
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:38,540
So you just went and bought
a cruiser all of a sudden?

377
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:44,240
You, who play life by the sacrifice bunt, pulling off a steal of
home with two outs and the bases loaded in the bottom of the ninth.

378
00:25:44,820 --> 00:25:47,880
Next time, Papa, you're Wakadaishō, okay?

379
00:25:56,100 --> 00:25:56,460
Thanks.

